      "reason": "SOL keeps his weary acknowledgment that he has done enough."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H031",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Hollow words fell from his lips” preserves the empty, quiet delivery."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H032",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The familiarity detail is retained in H033, so deleting this fragment loses no fact."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H033",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL retains their shared battles, familiar faces, visible gaps, and low death toll."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H034",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves the counterfactual and the likely deaths of more than half the survivors."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H035",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“That was no exaggeration” keeps the reference clear from the preceding claim."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H036",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Brought … to a swift victory” preserves the battle’s rapid resolution and reduced bloodshed."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H037",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“All on his own” preserves the source’s emphasis that he finished the historic battle alone."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H038",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves his forced-open eyes and westward gaze in natural phrasing."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H039",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The light remaining in his eyes is preserved without an unnecessary subject repetition."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H040",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Following” preserves the gaze pursuing someone no longer visible."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H041",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Foretold” naturally conveys the land’s darkness foreshadowing the coming war."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H042",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Resolve” is a natural rendering of 의지 here and preserves the thought’s sense of duty."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H043",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Keep moving” preserves the imperative to advance without changing the meaning."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H044",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Before long” naturally preserves the not-too-distant future."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H045",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves that his depleted mental strength can no longer move his body."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H046",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Gave way” makes explicit the legs’ failure, while preserving the chest pain and its effect."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H047",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“On his second step” preserves the timing of the wall he hits."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H048",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The adjusted sentence order preserves the tilting vision and impending blackout."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H049",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Hauled” and “broke through” preserve the rescue and the voices reaching him."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H050",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Now he knew” preserves his realization about the hand and the solid object."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H051",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean includes a distinct 까득 sound before his vision clears; deleting it drops an audible beat."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H052",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL replaces the vision clearing with clenching his teeth, a different physical action."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H053",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves the vision clearing, swallowed blood, and welcome faces; “two” is supported by context."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H054",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves the laugh and the Skeleton King’s stiff expression."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H055",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL keeps the insult and the question about Jin’s sanity without changing the joke."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H056",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Stupid things” preserves the rebuke in natural dialogue."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H057",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The Skeleton King is holding up one finger; the singular matches the scene."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H058",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL drops the instruction to stop waving the finger and lower it; BASE preserves both actions."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H059",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL clarifies whose face the middle finger was waved in front of without changing the action."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H060",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Snorted” preserves the quiet, amused reaction before the cough."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H061",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL changes the stammered start “Team Leader Choi…” into “Team…” and shifts the cough’s timing."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H062",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“A little injured, but fine” preserves the reassurance without redundant phrasing."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H063",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean explicitly says he let out a relieved sigh, not merely a breath."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H064",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Short of breath” naturally preserves his ragged breathing and dull senses."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H065",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The past-tense phrasing preserves the idea that a small gesture or word conveyed everything."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H066",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves Magic Johnson’s intuitive understanding and response without repeating Jin’s name."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H067",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Expression hardened” preserves the change in his face."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H068",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“And I know” naturally continues Johnson’s reply and preserves the added point."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H069",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL retains the Grand Mage’s clear perception, Jin’s limit, and his effort to stay conscious."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H070",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves the continuation of the thought about recklessness belonging to youth."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H071",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The Korean is a direct request; removing “Please” preserves its force."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H072",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Then leave” naturally conveys Johnson’s threat to resign."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H073",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean says Jin continued speaking; SOL omits that continuation cue."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H074",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“At a loss for words” naturally conveys that Johnson could not speak."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H075",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "The play-on-words explanation is retained in H076, so deleting this duplicate loses no content."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H076",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL retains the clumsy resignation-and-orders exchange and the truth of Jin’s resolve and duty."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H077",
      "decision": "REPAIR",
      "replacement": "He couldn’t bring himself to meet those eyes. He was ashamed of himself for having to make this choice.",
      "reason": "Both versions make the shame awkwardly about having no choice; the Korean says he was ashamed of himself for making this choice."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H078",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves Johnson squeezing his eyes shut, opening them, and gritting his teeth."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H079",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Teleporting” naturally preserves the danger of using Teleport in the high magical-power concentration."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H080",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Gave a faint smile” preserves the subdued expression."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H081",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL drops the emphasis in 보기 좋게, that they succeeded impressively; BASE preserves it with “just fine.”"
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H082",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Told us about at the beginning” naturally preserves the location being revealed earlier."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H083",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean specifies his pupils trembling; SOL changes that physical detail to his eyes."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H084",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean repeats that he definitely had to stop Jin; “He knew he had to” weakens that insistence."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H085",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“His damned Grand Mage’s mind” preserves the exasperation and the calculation."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H086",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves the prior Teleport attempt during the Arch Lich battle."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H087",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Among the finest mages alive” preserves Johnson’s exceptional ability."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H088",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL drops “magic” from the established term Teleport magic."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H089",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "SOL preserves both the recklessness of the proposal and the unavoidable reality behind it."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H090",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Was almost impossible” preserves the near-impossibility of catching the Doppelganger."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H091",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL drops “magic” from the established term Teleport magic."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H092",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL drops “magic” from the established term Teleport magic."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H093",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "SOL adds that this changed everything; the Korean only makes the preceding conclusion cruel."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H094",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean explicitly says Jin stands without anyone’s help; SOL omits that detail."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H095",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Beside Jin” clearly preserves the companion’s position and volunteered participation."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H096",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Stay and protect this place” preserves the instruction without unnecessary repetition."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H097",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“Knew he had nowhere left to retreat” preserves Johnson’s realization."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H098",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "The Korean says his voice rang out faintly; SOL changes that to merely sounding faint."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H099",
      "decision": "SOL",
      "reason": "“No matter what” naturally preserves the insistence in 반드시."
    },
    {
      "hunk_id": "H100",
      "decision": "BASE",
      "reason": "“Overwhelming” preserves the immense flash; “blinding” changes its effect."
    }
  ]
}

